\**{c=red:Note:}** Having a significant amount of Rancor (Tonberry enmity) can be very harmful as the mission requires you to combat several {p:Tonberries|Tonberry}, including {p:Notorious Monsters} that can use the ability **Everyone's Rancor** for a great amount of damage. The rancor can be lowered with the quest {p:Everyone's Grudge} located in {z:Norg}. Consider completing this before proceeding.
* One can avoid gaining rancor by calling for help as well.

=2 Shortcut
* If you already have the Den of Rancor Home Point unlocked, you can use it to warp directly to the Den of Rancor, step into the Sacrificial Chamber, and enter the Battlefield for the boss fight.
* A player who has already completed this mission can use the home point and open the door for you, allowing you to skip the puzzle entirely. Use the Unity Warp (level 128) to reach the door if you are using this method.

=2 Walkthrough
!Temple of Uggalepih Composite.png|right|Composite Map
!Den of Rancor-map1.jpg|right|Den Map 1
!Den of Rancor-map2.jpg|right|Den Map 2
The overall goal of this mission is to reach the {z:Sacrificial Chamber} BCNM zone. Before that, your goal is to reach the {z:Den of Rancor}.
>**__Reaching the Den of Rancor**__
>**Method #1**
Use the {z:Den of Rancor} {p:Home Point} #1 warp.
If you have the {p:Home Point} already, you can simply warp there and zone into the {z:Sacrificial Chamber} area.
>**Method #2**
The {p:Unity} warp to {z:Den of Rancor} (under content level 128) allows you to skip the {z:Temple of Uggalepih} step of **Method #3** without the need for a {@k}{k:Paintbrush of souls}.
\**{c=red:Note}**: You will still need an {@i:Unlit Lantern|1138} {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138}, unless somebody opens the Rancor door for you. **Anyone with the {p:Home Point} warp can easily do this, saving you a lot of time.**
>**Method #3**
This is the old fashioned way, by obtaining the {@k}{k:Paintbrush of souls}.
See the {k:Mini-Quest|Paintbrush of souls} page for instructions on obtaining the item, then come back to this page and continue below:
You will also need one {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} to access the {z:Sacrificial Chamber} area. Obtain one via the below methods, and continue on the {z:Temple of Uggalepih} steps.
{i:Unlit Lanterns|Unlit Lantern|1138} are dropped by {m:Tonberry Jinxers|Tonberry Jinxer} in {z:Yhoator Jungle}, {m:Tonberry Maledictors|Tonberry Maledictor} and {m:Tonberry Pursuers|Tonberry Pursuer} in {z:Temple of Uggalepih}, and slightly higher level {m:Tonberry Imprecators|Tonberry Imprecator} in {z:Den of Rancor}.
A good area to farm Maledictors would be the map with {m:Sozu Rogberry}'s **???** and where Uggalepih Offering can be found.
>**{z:Temple of Uggalepih} steps**
* Enter the Temple from the main entrance in {z:Yhoator Jungle} (J-11/12).
** The {p:Voidwatch} warp brings you to this entrance.
* Make your way to the northwestern exit at (F-5). Pick up the {p:Survival Guide} on the way.
** You will zone out into {z:Yhoator Jungle}. Make a left after zoning.
* Enter the temple again from (H-11), and work your way down to the {m:Temple Guardian} at (I-10).
** Kill the guardian if he is up, otherwise the door will be open already.
* Go ahead to (I-7). The door is on the far side of the room. Whoever has the {@k}{k:Paintbrush of souls} needs to stand at the empty frame in the middle of the wall. Everyone else wait by the door.
** To use the Paintbrush, check the frame and confirm you wish to continue. You should get a message saying "a new painting begins to appear on the canvas". Wait 30 seconds without moving or entering any commands, and check it again. You should get another message about the {z:Den of Rancor}, and the door will open.
** The person who is checking the frame cannot be aggro'd or acted on during these 30 seconds, otherwise you'll have to start over.

>**{z:Den of Rancor} steps**
* Enter the {z:Den of Rancor}. Everyone will need {s:Sneak} and {p:Invisible (Status)}.
* Head to (E-5) on map 1. Once clear of the bomb mobs there, drop Invisible and trade your {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} to the **Altar of Rancor**. You will receive a {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139} item instead.
* Run to (F-7) and drop down the hole in the northeast corner to map 2. Make your way to (E-5) on this new map.
* To access the {z:Sacrificial Chamber} the four lanterns outside its gate need to be lit with {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139} by trading the {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} to an **Altar of Rancor**. While it can be done with one {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} going back and forth from the Alter of Rancor and the lanterns, it would be suggested to farm multiple. 4 is ideal, but you can only hold one Lantern and one Flame at any time so that will require 4 players.
** Consider clearing the room, as it is hard to trade while being attacked.

>**After arriving at the {p:Home Point} in {z:Den of Rancor}**
* Be sure to obtain the Home Point, and then walk further to zone into the {z:Sacrificial Chamber}.
* Examine the door to progress to the boss fight, see below for details.
** The name of the fight is the same as the mission, **"The Temple of Uggalepih"**

=2 Boss Fight
* Inside, gather up and prepare. You will now enter an uncapped {p:BCNM} against 3 {p:Tonberry} NMs. Buff inside, as they'll wear upon entering the BC.
* Once you've cleared the BC, you'll get a cutscene. Afterwards, you'll exit on the other side of the {z:Sacrificial Chamber}, that will lead you back out to the Temple.
* After winning the BCNM, you may now continue {p:Rhapsodies of Vanadiel} Mission 2-24 {M:The Cursed Temple|The Cursed Temple|The Cursed Temple}.

[Area
{z:Sacrificial Chamber}
>Boss
{m:Grav'iton} (THF), {m:Molyb'iton} (BLM), and {m:Tungs'iton} (SMN)
>Abilities
* {m:Grav'iton}:
** Uses both {p:Perfect Dodge} and Everyone's Rancor.
* {m:Molyb'iton}:
** Uses {p:Manafont} at some point.
* {m:Tungs'iton}:
** Uses {p:Astral Flow} at some point, summoning an avatar to wreak havoc.

>Notes
* Recommended to battle order of Grav'iton THF > Molyb'iton BLM > Tungs'iton SMN
* Grav'iton cannot be slept, and therefore should be defeated first. {p:Silence} and {s:Sleep} the other two.
* Grav'iton can use Everyone's Rancor, which does 10 times the damage of {p:Everyone's Grudge}. A tank can very easily be KOed by this if they have significant rancor.
* The Summoner will have a pet, but that does not indicate what avatar it will use for {p:Astral Flow}. Defeat it quickly to try and avoid Astral Flow. It probably won't KO you if it does use it, but it will cause you some issues. Make sure everyone has full HP before attacking it.

